                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Samuel 18:5",
        "book": "2 Samuel",
        "chapter": 18,
        "verse": 5
      },
      {
        "text": "So the people went out into the field against Israel: and the battle was in the wood of Ephraim;",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 80,
            "end": 84,
            "text": "Josh. 17:18 (15–18)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 6,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Samuel 18:6",
        "book": "2 Samuel",
        "chapter": 18,
        "verse": 6
      },
      {
        "text": "Where the people of Israel were slain before the servants of David, and there was there a great slaughter that day of twenty thousand men.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 134,
            "end": 138
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 7,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Samuel 18:7",
        "book": "2 Samuel",
        "chapter": 18,
        "verse": 7
      },
      {
        "text": "For the battle was there scattered over the face of all the country: and the wood devoured more people that day than the sword devoured.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 8,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Samuel 18:8",
        "book": "2 Samuel",
        "chapter": 18,
        "verse": 8
      },
      {
        "text": "And Absalom met the servants of David. And Absalom rode upon a mule, and the mule went under the thick boughs of a great oak, and his head caught hold of the oak, and he was taken up between the heaven and the earth; and the mule that was under him went away.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 235,
            "end": 238
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 9,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Samuel 18:9",
        "book": "2 Samuel",
        "chapter": 18,
        "verse": 9
      },
      {
        "text": "And a certain man saw it, and told Joab, and said, Behold, I saw Absalom hanged in an oak.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 22,
            "end": 25
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 10,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Samuel 18:10",
        "book": "2 Samuel",
        "chapter": 18,
        "verse": 10
      },
      {
        "text": "And Joab said unto the man that told him, And, behold, thou sawest him, and why didst thou not smite him there to the ground? and I would have given thee ten shekels of silver, and a girdle.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 67,
            "end": 71
          },
          {
            "start": 158,
            "end": 165
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 11,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Samuel 18:11",
        "book": "2 Samuel",
        "chapter": 18,
        "verse": 11
      },
      {
        "text": "And the man said unto Joab, Though I should receive a thousand shekels of silver in mine hand, yet would I not put forth mine hand against the king’s son: for in our hearing the king charged thee and Abishai and Ittai, saying, Beware that none touch the young man Absalom.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 183,
            "end": 190,
            "text": "2 Sam. 18:5."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 63,
            "end": 70
          },
          {
            "start": 95,
            "end": 98
          },
          {
            "start": 244,
            "end": 249
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 12,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "2 Sam. 18:5.",
            "prettyString": "2 Samuel 18:5",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "2samuel",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 18,
                    "end": 18,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 5,
                        "end": 5
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Samuel 18:12",
        "book": "2 Samuel",
        "chapter": 18,
        "verse": 12
      },
      {
        "text": "Otherwise I should have wrought falsehood against mine own life: for there is no matter hid from the king, and thou thyself wouldest have set thyself against me.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 158,
            "end": 161
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 13,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Samuel 18:13",
        "book": "2 Samuel",
        "chapter": 18,
        "verse": 13
      },
      {
        "text": "Then said Joab, I may not tarry thus with thee. And he took three darts in his hand, and thrust them through the heart of Absalom, while he was yet alive in the midst of the oak.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 140,
            "end": 143
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 14,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Samuel 18:14",
        "book": "2 Samuel",
        "chapter": 18,
        "verse": 14
      },
      {
        "text": "And ten young men that bare Joab’s armour compassed about and smote Absalom, and slew him.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 15,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Samuel 18:15",
        "book": "2 Samuel",
        "chapter": 18,
        "verse": 15
      },
      {
        "text": "And Joab blew the trumpet, and the people returned from pursuing after Israel: for Joab held back the people.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 16,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Samuel 18:16",
        "book": "2 Samuel",
        "chapter": 18,
        "verse": 16
      },
      {
        "text": "And they took Absalom, and cast him into a great pit in the wood, and laid a very great heap of stones upon him: and all Israel fled every one to his tent.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 17,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Samuel 18:17",
        "book": "2 Samuel",
        "chapter": 18,
        "verse": 17
      },
      {
        "text": "Now Absalom in his lifetime had taken and reared up for himself a pillar, which is in the king’s dale: for he said, I have no son to keep my name in remembrance: and he called the pillar after his own name: and it is called unto this day, Absalom’s place.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 90,
            "end": 96,
            "text": "Gen. 14:17."
          },
          {
            "start": 126,
            "end": 129,
            "text": "2 Sam. 14:27."
          },
          {
            "start": 249,
            "end": 254,
            "text": "OR monument."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 80,
            "end": 82
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 18,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Gen. 14:17.",
            "prettyString": "Genesis 14:17",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "genesis",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 14,
