          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Samuel 18:18",
        "book": "2 Samuel",
        "chapter": 18,
        "verse": 18
      },
      {
        "text": "Then said Ahimaaz the son of Zadok, Let me now run, and bear the king tidings, how that the Lord hath avenged him of his enemies.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 19,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Samuel 18:19",
        "book": "2 Samuel",
        "chapter": 18,
        "verse": 19
      },
      {
        "text": "And Joab said unto him, Thou shalt not bear tidings this day, but thou shalt bear tidings another day: but this day thou shalt bear no tidings, because the king’s son is dead.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 20,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Samuel 18:20",
        "book": "2 Samuel",
        "chapter": 18,
        "verse": 20
      },
      {
        "text": "Then said Joab to Cushi, Go tell the king what thou hast seen. And Cushi bowed himself unto Joab, and ran.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 21,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Samuel 18:21",
        "book": "2 Samuel",
        "chapter": 18,
        "verse": 21
      },
      {
        "text": "Then said Ahimaaz the son of Zadok yet again to Joab, But howsoever, let me, I pray thee, also run after Cushi. And Joab said, Wherefore wilt thou run, my son, seeing that thou hast no tidings ready?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 22,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Samuel 18:22",
        "book": "2 Samuel",
        "chapter": 18,
        "verse": 22
      },
      {
        "text": "But howsoever, said he, let me run. And he said unto him, Run. Then Ahimaaz ran by the way of the plain, and overran Cushi.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 15,
            "end": 23
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 23,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Samuel 18:23",
        "book": "2 Samuel",
        "chapter": 18,
        "verse": 23
      },
      {
        "text": "And David sat between the two gates: and the watchman went up to the roof over the gate unto the wall, and lifted up his eyes, and looked, and behold a man running alone.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 24,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Samuel 18:24",
        "book": "2 Samuel",
        "chapter": 18,
        "verse": 24
      },
      {
        "text": "And the watchman cried, and told the king. And the king said, If he be alone, there is tidings in his mouth. And he came apace, and drew near.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 68,
            "end": 70
          },
          {
            "start": 78,
            "end": 86
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 25,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Samuel 18:25",
        "book": "2 Samuel",
        "chapter": 18,
        "verse": 25
      },
      {
        "text": "And the watchman saw another man running: and the watchman called unto the porter, and said, Behold another man running alone. And the king said, He also bringeth tidings.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 100,
            "end": 107
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 26,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Samuel 18:26",
        "book": "2 Samuel",
        "chapter": 18,
        "verse": 26
      },
      {
        "text": "And the watchman said, Me thinketh the running of the foremost is like the running of Ahimaaz the son of Zadok. And the king said, He is a good man, and cometh with good tidings.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 134,
            "end": 136
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 27,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Samuel 18:27",
        "book": "2 Samuel",
        "chapter": 18,
        "verse": 27
      },
      {
        "text": "And Ahimaaz called, and said unto the king, All is well. And he fell down to the earth upon his face before the king, and said, Blessed be the Lord thy God, which hath delivered up the men that lifted up their hand against my lord the king.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 136,
            "end": 138
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 28,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Samuel 18:28",
        "book": "2 Samuel",
        "chapter": 18,
        "verse": 28
      },
      {
        "text": "And the king said, Is the young man Absalom safe? And Ahimaaz answered, When Joab sent the king’s servant, and me thy servant, I saw a great tumult, but I knew not what it was.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 19,
            "end": 21
          },
          {
            "start": 111,
            "end": 113
          },
          {
            "start": 169,
            "end": 176
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 29,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Samuel 18:29",
        "book": "2 Samuel",
        "chapter": 18,
        "verse": 29
      },
      {
        "text": "And the king said unto him, Turn aside, and stand here. And he turned aside, and stood still.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 18,
            "end": 27
          },
          {
            "start": 40,
            "end": 43
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 30,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Samuel 18:30",
        "book": "2 Samuel",
        "chapter": 18,
        "verse": 30
      },
      {
        "text": "And, behold, Cushi came; and Cushi said, Tidings, my lord the king: for the Lord hath avenged thee this day of all them that rose up against thee.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 31,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Samuel 18:31",
        "book": "2 Samuel",
        "chapter": 18,
        "verse": 31
      },
      {
        "text": "And the king said unto Cushi, Is the young man Absalom safe? And Cushi answered, The enemies of my lord the king, and all that rise against thee to do thee hurt, be as that young man is.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 30,
            "end": 32
          },
          {
            "start": 151,
            "end": 155
          },
          {
            "start": 168,
            "end": 172
          },
          {
            "start": 183,
            "end": 186
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 32,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Samuel 18:32",
        "book": "2 Samuel",
        "chapter": 18,
        "verse": 32
      },
      {
        "text": "And the king was much moved, and went up to the chamber over the gate, and wept: and as he went, thus he said, O my son Absalom, my son, my son Absalom! would God I had died for thee, O Absalom, my son, my son!",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 33,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Samuel 18:33",
